{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.BerezinianBarOddIsolation","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.BerezinianBarOddIsolation","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Hom.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BerezinianBarOddIsolation.barEven_diagonal_invisible_to_barOdd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BerezinianBarOddIsolation.barEven_diagonal_invisible_to_barOdd","kind":"theorem","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BerezinianBarOddIsolation.lean#L40-L46","doc":"**Even diagonal drops out of the bar-odd face (sum form).** For any bar-even `A`, adding\n`A` to a cross-term `t` leaves the bar-odd part exactly unchanged: `(A + t) − σ(A + t) =\nt − σt` (an exact equality, no sign convention). The bar-even mass is invisible to the decay\n(bar-odd) channel. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BerezinianBarOddIsolation.barOdd_M_eq_neg_barOdd_crossTerm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BerezinianBarOddIsolation.barOdd_M_eq_neg_barOdd_crossTerm","kind":"theorem","line":32,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BerezinianBarOddIsolation.lean#L32-L38","doc":"**Bar-odd isolation.** For the mass endomorphism `𝓜 = A − t` with bar-even diagonal\n`A` (`σA = A`), the bar-odd part `𝓜 − σ𝓜` equals `−(t − σt)` — minus the cross-term's\nbar-odd part, with **no** contribution from the diagonal mass `A`. So `c₃` (the bar-odd\nface) is carried entirely by the cross-term `t = B·D⁻¹·C`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}